module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.NagataRing
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Defs

/-!
# Finite algebras over Nagata rings

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Lemma Tag 032T, finite case
of the quasi-finite-over-Nagata lemma (blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-finite-over-nagata-nagata).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

/-- If `R` is Nagata and `S` is finite as an `R`-algebra, then `S` is Nagata;
quotients of `R` by arbitrary ideals are Nagata as well.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tag 032T, finite case, using Tag 032I.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-finite-over-nagata-nagata).

Proof:
1. The finite algebra `S` is Noetherian by `lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-noetherian`
   and `def-weil-pbc-nagata-ring`. For a prime `q` of `S`, contract it to `p` in `R`.
   The induced map `A = R/p → B = S/q` is injective between domains, and the images
   of module generators of `S` generate `B` over `A`
   (`def-weil-finitely-generated-module`). The quotient `A` is Noetherian by the same
   finite-algebra lemma and N-2 by the Nagata hypothesis.
2. Put `K = Frac(A)` and `L = Frac(B)`. Localizing `B` at the nonzero elements of `A`
   gives a nonzero finite-dimensional `K`-domain, hence a field by
   `lem-weil-pbc-finite-dimensional-domain-is-field`. This field is `L`, since it contains
   `B` and the inverses of its nonzero elements. Thus `L/K` is finite
   (`def-pc-field-extension`). Every finite extension `M/L` is finite over `K` by
   `lem-weil-pbc-field-degree-multiplicativity`.
3. The integral closure of `A` in `M` is finite over `A` by N-2
   (`def-weil-pbc-japanese-domain`, `def-weil-pbc-integral-closure`). Since `B/A` is
   finite, it is integral by `lem-weil-pbc-finite-algebra-is-integral`. Transitivity
   (`lem-weil-pbc-integral-transitive`) shows that the integral closures of `A` and `B`
   in `M` agree; conversely, a monic polynomial over `A` is also one over `B`.
   The same finite generators over `A` generate this closure over `B`. Therefore `B`
   is N-2 for every prime `q`, so Noetherianity gives `IsNagataRing S`.
4. For any ideal `I` of `R`, the quotient `R/I` is finite over `R`, generated by `1`
   (`def-weil-finitely-generated-module`). Apply the finite-algebra result to this map. -/
theorem finite_over_nagata_is_nagata (R : Type u) (S : Type v) [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [Module.Finite R S] (hR : IsNagataRing R) :
    IsNagataRing S ∧ ∀ (I : Ideal R), IsNagataRing (R ⧸ I) := by
  sorry
